# Contributor setup

A PR into `next` gets its body from `node .agents/pstack/land.mjs`. An agent that writes the body itself runs a stale setup, so this skill fixes the setup once, and later PRs pass the body check.

1. Run `node .agents/rules/contributor-setup/scripts/doctor.mjs` from the repository root. It fetches `next`, changes nothing else, and prints a `stale:` line with its `fix:` for each part of the setup behind `next`, then a `pr:` line for each of your open PRs into `next` whose body check failed.
2. Apply each `fix:` in the order printed, from the directory it names. A fix that needs the human, such as trusting a folder or Codex's hooks, goes to them as one line, and you wait for their word. A `claude plugin` command run from the checkout may rewrite `.claude/settings.json`, whose pin belongs to the repository, so restore that file when `git diff .claude/settings.json` shows a change.
3. A merge of `next` loads its instructions only in a new session. After that fix, ask the human to start one with this skill, and stop here.
4. Run the doctor again. This step is done when it prints `ok:` and no `stale:` line.
5. Rewrite each `pr:` body the way `land.mjs` would. Save it with `gh pr view <number> --json body --jq .body > <file>`. When the PR changes exactly one plan under `docs/plans/`, render that plan into the file as the `plan-page` skill's PR section says, with `--into <file>`. Otherwise keep the body, add a short paragraph on why the change exists, and end it with a line that starts `Beyond the ask:` and names each change the request did not ask for, or says `none`. Update the PR with `gh pr edit <number> --body-file <file>`, and the check runs again. This step is done when the doctor prints no `pr:` line.

Land later changes with `land.mjs`, as `.agents/pstack/rules/land.md` says. It opens the PR into `next` with the right body.
